  "strategy": "Approach and rationale:\nWe will use a hierarchical optimization method that combines coarse-grained population-based search with fine-grained local optimization. Starting from a low-resolution grid, the algorithm explores promising regions using differential evolution (DE) and then refines solutions via sequential resolution increases (grid doubling) followed by constrained optimization. This approach balances exploration (DE) and exploitation (local optimization) while naturally addressing the high dimensionality of the problem. The rationale is that DE can uncover global patterns at coarse grids that local methods might miss, while grid refinement preserves solution quality and convergence while the penalty function ensures constraint satisfaction.\n\nMathematical specification:\nMinimize max_{k} \u222b h(x)(1-h(x+k)) dx over x\u2208[0,2]\nsubject to:\n0 \u2264 h(x) \u2264 1, \u222b h(x) dx = 1\nDiscretization: h \u2208 \u211d^n, dx = 2/n, \u2211_{i=1}^n h_i = n/2\n\nImplementation procedure:\n1. Initial setup:\n   - Validate input_grid (if provided)\n   - Convert grid to length n0 (min=100, max=500)\n   - Initialize best_val = \u221e, best_h = None\n2. Coarse selection phase:\n   - Sample initial population: \n        h_uniform = np.linspace(0,n/2,size=n0)  # Initial guess for grid doubling\n        h_opt = differential_evolution(objective, [0,1], np.array([0.5]*n0))  # DE for the coarse grid\n3. Progressive resolution refinement:\n   - For each doubling in grid size (n_i = n_{i-1}*2):\n        \u2022 Evaluate current population with DE\n        \u2022 Project to feasible space via penalty: \n            obj_h(h) = max_koverlap + penalty(|\u2211h| - n/2| + max_i|h_i|>1)\n        \u2022 Use local optimization: \n            minimize obj(h) subject to Ax=b (integral constraint) \n        \u2022 Store best candidate from local phase\n4. Python code outline:\n   from scipy.optimize import differential_evolution, minimize\n   def objective(h):\n       dx = 2/ len(h)\n       corr = np.correlate(h, 1-h, mode='full')\n       return np.max(corr) * dx + penalty(h)\n   def project_feasible(h, n):\n       if np.all(h>=0) and np.all(h<=1):\n           return h\n       # Compute gradient projection for integral constraint\n       target = n/2\n       grad = finite_difference(np.gradient, h)\n       adjustment = (target - sum(h))/n  \n       h_adjusted = np.clip(h + grad * adjustment, 0, 1)\n       return project_feasible(h_adjusted, n)\n5. Hybrid refinement strategy:\n   - DE runs use population size=50, max evals=10000\n   - Local optimization uses SLSQP with constr=[{'type':'eq', 'fun': lambda h: sum(h)-n/2}]\n   - Grid doubling triggers 3-phase refinement: DE > SLSQP > project_feasible\n   - Early termination if improvement stalls by 1e-6\n   - Budget allocation: 40% to coarse grid, 60% to refinement\n\nSearch choices and variations:\n- Radius: [10, 100] results in best improvement rates\n- DE mutation factor: {'rand/1': 0.8, 'rand/2': None}\n- Local phase: {'SLSQP': {'maxiter': 1000}, 'COBYLA': {'maxiter': 500}}\n- Priority lists: {'DE': [0.7, 0.8, 0.9], 'SLPQS: [0.5, 0.6, 0.4]}\n- Refinement: [2, 4, 8] doublings, but limited by budget\n\nCompute budget and robustness:\n- Total budget: 1100 seconds distributed as DE (600s), grid scan (300s), local (200s)\n- Time monitoring: Before each expensive op check elapsed time\n- Warm restarts: Every 300s use median values from current population\n- Null-handle: If invalid values (NaN or \u221e), return previous best\n- Fallback: Keep parent solution if refinement fails\n\nValidation and return contract:\n- Input: grid of n samples (0\u2264h_i\u22641, \u2211h_i=n/2)\n- Checks: Validate integral constraint (tol=5e-3), feasible bounds\n- Return: (h_improved, c5_value, final_n)\n- Score computation: np.max(np.correlate(h,1-h,mode='full'))*(2/len(h))\n\nThis approach ensures continuous improvement across scales with mathematically sound constraint handling while remaining within resource limits.",
